---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Terms of Service — pipper"
    description="Terms of service for using the pipper code website and the Pipper Code desktop application."
    pageClass="legal-page"
>
    <article class="legal-shell w-full max-w-[46rem] mx-auto px-[clamp(1.25rem,4vw,2rem)] pt-12 md:pt-16 pb-20 flex flex-col gap-6 font-geist">
        <header class="legal-head flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h1 class="font-medium text-[clamp(1.8rem,4.5vw,3rem)] tracking-[-0.035em] leading-[1.1]">
                Terms of Service
            </h1>
            <p class="text-[0.85rem] opacity-60">Last updated: August 9, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="legal-body text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.7] min-w-0">
            <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
            <p>
                These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the pipper website
                (pipper.dev, including its subdomains) and the Pipper Code desktop application
                (together, the "Service"), operated by the pipper team. By using the Service, you
                agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Using the Service</h2>
            <p>
                You may use the Service for your own purposes, including commercial work. You agree
                not to misuse it: you will not attempt to disrupt, reverse-engineer, or interfere
                with the Service, or use it in any way that violates applicable law.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Accounts and Authentication</h2>
            <p>
                Certain features of the Service require you to sign in. Authentication is provided
                through Clerk and tied to an account you control with your chosen identity provider.
                You are responsible for safeguarding your credentials and for activity that happens
                under your account.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Your Content</h2>
            <p>
                The Software runs AI coding agents that may read, write, and execute against files
                and codebases on your machine. That work stays local to your device and is yours.
                You are solely responsible for the prompts you give agents, the actions you approve,
                and any content or code you produce with the Service. We do not claim ownership of
                your content.
            </p>

            <h2>5. No Warranty</h2>
            <p>
                The Service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
                express or implied. The Software is currently in alpha. We do not warrant that the
                Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that agents will produce safe or
                correct results. You use the Service at your own risk.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
            <p>
                To the fullest extent permitted by law, the pipper team shall not be liable for any
                indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of
                profits or data, arising from or relating to your use of the Service — including
                any code, changes, or other output agents produce.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Changes</h2>
            <p>
                We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by
                updating the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of the Service after changes
                take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Questions about these Terms can be directed to the pipper team via the Discord
                server linked from the site, or through our public GitHub repository.
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</Layout>

<style>
    :global(.legal-page) {
        background: #f0efed !important;
        color: #111111 !important;
    }
    .legal-shell h2 {
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        font-weight: 620;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    .legal-shell p { color: rgb(17 17 17 / 0.78); }
</style>